<text top="160" left="107" width="703" height="16" font="1">The energy estimate leaves one fact settled: the kinetic energy stays finite throughout the</text>
<text top="182" left="108" width="702" height="16" font="1">maximal smooth interval. That control does not stop the velocity from changing more</text>
<text top="203" left="108" width="702" height="16" font="1">sharply across shorter distances. Viscosity is the part of the equation we expect to stop that</text>
<text top="225" left="108" width="552" height="16" font="1">sharpening. It acts alongside the three other pieces of the same motion:</text>
